#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wallhaven browsing and palette helper for Island.

Every subcommand prints JSON on stdout (``previews`` prints one JSON object per
line) and exits non-zero with ``{"error": ...}`` on failure.  The API key is
only ever read from Island's private state file, ``ISLAND_WALLHAVEN_NEW_KEY``
(``set-key``) or Aether's config, and is sent in the ``X-API-Key`` header so it
never appears in argv, URLs or logs.

Usage:
  wallhaven config
  wallhaven save-config JSON
  wallhaven set-key                  (key in ISLAND_WALLHAVEN_NEW_KEY, empty clears)
  wallhaven search JSON
  wallhaven info ID
  wallhaven collections USER
  wallhaven collection USER ID [PAGE [cache]]
  wallhaven thumbs JSON              (cache thumbnails on disk, one {id,path} line each)
  wallhaven prepare ID [URL]         (download the full image into the cache)
  wallhaven install ID [URL [NAME]]  (move it into the Dynamic wallpaper library)
  wallhaven rename-file PATH NAME    (rename a library wallpaper, keeping its extension)
  wallhaven library                  (list the Dynamic wallpaper library)
  wallhaven previews PATH dark|light (one line per scheme)
  wallhaven preview PATH SCHEME dark|light
  wallhaven palette-file PATH SCHEME dark|light OUT.toml
  wallhaven schemes
"""
